  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Sunday)\n\nDry pattern looks to continue through the week as Nevada remains \nunder southwesterly flow aloft. The upper pattern looks to remain \nconsistent for the week as a series of upper level troughs pass \nthrough the Pacific NW. This active pattern to our north will keep\na very low 10% to 15% chance of light showers across the ID/OR/NV\nborder as each trough passes through, this will keep temperatures\nclose to seasonal for this time of year, yet winds over central \nNevada elevated which will bring fire weather concerns for \nTuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday for the US 50 Corridor. \nTemperatures for the week will run in the upper 70s to upper 80s \nfor highs, with overnight lows in the upper 30s to upper 40s. \nWinds for northern Nevada will be out of the west to southwest at \n5 to 15 MPH with gusts up to 25 MPH. For central Nevada winds will\nbe stronger out of the southwest at 20 to 35 MPH with gusts up to\n45 MPH possible. Combined with low RH values in the afternoons \nthis will lead to elevated to near critical fire weather concerns \nfor White Pine, N Nye, S Eureka, and S Lander counties mid week. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence in dry conditions with seasonal \ntemperatures continuing through the week. \n\nThere is high confidence in breezy to strong SW winds Tuesday \nthrough Thursday for central Nevada as an upper trough passes \nthrough OR/ID.\n\nThere is low confidence in a 10% to 15% chance for isolated \nshowers Wednesday through Thursday for far northern Nevada.",
